<Article
  title="Free food, free water, paid for by the label"
  description="Aura hopes to build a network where food and water from the shells are free to take, because advertisers pay to put their name on the harvest and the jug."
  kicker="The hope"
  date="2026-09-30"
>
  <p>The farm units can already be asked for. H20, the water unit, comes later and still needs further research. The network around either of them does not exist yet. This note is that hope, written so it cannot be mistaken for a signup.</p>
  <h2>The exchange</h2>
  <p>A person takes food, or a jug of water, and does not pay. An advertiser has paid to put their name on that food or that jug. The payment is what pays the person who runs the shell. Aura’s role, if the network is built, is the advertising placement and the shells, not a toll on the person who is thirsty or hungry.</p>
  <p>The same shell can skip the network. An owner who buys a farm wall can keep the harvest. A bottling line, once H20 is past research, could be used the same way. The franchise is a choice we want to offer later. The farm unit is the choice available to ask about now.</p>
  <h2>What “franchise” means here</h2>
  <p>It means a repeated way to place shells, fill jugs, harvest a wall, and carry an advertiser’s label under one set of rules. It does not mean a territory for sale, a fee schedule, or a brand you can license this month. There is no advertiser marketplace on this site. There is no token, and there is no wallet, on the <a href="/builder">builder</a> either.</p>
  <h2>Why say it now</h2>
  <p>The rooms, the <a href="/farms">farm walls</a>, and the <a href="/water">water unit</a> are easier to understand if the longer aim is visible. People who only want a room should still be able to find the room, and stop there. People who want to grow can ask for a farm unit and ignore the network. People who want water from the air can read the H20 page and wait for the research. People who want to help build the free distribution can enquire with that aim named.</p>
  <p>Until an advertiser has actually paid, and a jug has actually been given away, the honest sentence is the one above: this is what we hope to accomplish.</p>
</Article>
